    "title": "Smuggling charges against NIH virologists trigger political uproar - Nature",
    "snippet": "Two virologists at the US National Institutes of Health (NIH) are facing charges related to the alleged smuggling of non-infectious monkeypox virus (MPXV) and other biological samples into the United States, in a case that has become a flashpoint for legal and political concerns around biosecurity. The charges centre on samples that NIH scientists Vincent Munster and Claude Kwe were carrying when they arrived in Detroit, Michigan, in January after doing research in the Republic of the Congo. According to the complaint, which was brought by the US Department of Justice, Munster and Kwe allegedly failed to declare the samples and then lied to officials about them. The case is the latest in a string of prosecutions of researchers for smuggling biological samples. It has brought additional scrutiny to Munster and Kwe\u2019s workplace, the NIH\u2019s Rocky Mountain Lab (RML), in Hamilton, Montana, and to the import of pathogens for study.",
